## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: hat, Language: Haitian Creole, Number of verses: 21
## References: Bakker, P., Daval-Markussen, A., Parkvall, M., & Plag, I. (2011). Creoles are typologically distinct from non-creoles. Journal of Pidgin and Creole Languages, 26(1), 5–42. ; Encyclopaedia Britannica. (2026). Haitian Creole. Encyclopaedia Britannica.
## Contributors: # AN QING: an0026ng AT e DOT ntu DOT edu DOT sg #

